meta {
  name: Refresh Token
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
  }
}

docs {
  # Refresh Access Token

  Get a new access token using the refresh token.

  ## When to Use
  - When your access token expires (after 7 days / 10,080 minutes)
  - To get a new token without re-authenticating with Google

  ## Request Body
  ```json
  {
    "refresh_token": "your_refresh_token_here"
  }
  ```

  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "access_token": "new_access_token",
    "token_type": "bearer",
    "expires_in": 604800
  }
  ```

  ## Steps
  1. Ensure you have a valid refresh_token in {{refreshToken}}
  2. Send this request
  3. Copy the new access_token
  4. Update {{accessToken}} with the new value
  5. Continue using authenticated endpoints

  ## Error Responses
  - **401 Unauthorized**: Refresh token is invalid or expired
  - **404 Not Found**: User not found
  - **403 Forbidden**: User account is inactive
}
